https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VUv_YSQV0c4  (Capo 2)

Also in (G) which may be easier to play without the pinky stretch on the (DaddA) and without the (Bm) but you'll have to capo 9 to play along with the recording.

If transposing, play the transposed (DaddA) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  Transcribing piano to guitar can always be a bit dodgy but for the first part of the intro, form (DaddA) by extending your pinky over to the 1st string of the 5th fret from normal (D).  Now strum the chord once downward from the 4th string to the 1st string (individual notes may or may not transpose).  As soon as you hit the 1st string lift off completely and include open 1st string while moving quickly over to the (A) to mute the overtones.  So there are 5 notes total.  Then strum (A) once and quickly jump to the (G) and back to the (A).  For the second part of the intro just play the majors.  If this is all too messy and inconvenient just play the first part like the second using the major chords. 
    

